<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γερᾰρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of reverend bearing, majestic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.170
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραρώτερος ἦεν
			Ὀδυσσεύς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				211
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραρὴ τράπεζα</span> a table
				<i>of honour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Xenoph.
				1.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραραῖς χερσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.818
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ γ. τὸ εἶδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ γ. τοῦ ἤθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					1.15
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς, μέλπουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.692
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραιός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				722
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. τοκῆες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.1335
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				9.90
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραροί, οἱ</span>, <i>elders</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				667
			</span></i> (lyr.); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραραί</span>
			<i>priestesses of Dionysus</i> is f. l. for
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέραιραι</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				D.
				59.73
			</span></i>, al.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μητρὸς . . πρόπολος σεμνή τε γέραιρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.2116
				</span></i>
			, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραίρας</span> (acc. pl.) is
			prob. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.270
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				287
			</span></i> (cf. Sch. BT); cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				227.35
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέραιρα</span> old fem. of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεραρός</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χίμαιρα</span>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χίμαρος</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
